Neural network models (downloaded on demand into ~/.texelith/models)
-------------------------------------------------------------------
MiDaS v2.1 Small
  Intel Intelligent Systems Lab — https://github.com/isl-org/MiDaS
  Ranftl et al., "Towards Robust Monocular Depth Estimation: Mixing Datasets
  for Zero-shot Cross-dataset Transfer".
  Licence: MIT.

Depth Anything V2 Small
  Yang et al., "Depth Anything V2", 2024 —
  https://github.com/DepthAnything/Depth-Anything-V2
  ONNX export: https://github.com/fabio-sim/Depth-Anything-ONNX
  Licence: Apache License 2.0 (the Small model; larger variants are
  CC-BY-NC-4.0 and are not used).

1x NormalMapGenerator-CX-Lite
1x FrankenMapGenerator-CX-Lite
  Author: Joey (JoeyBallentine) —
  https://github.com/joeyballentine/Material-Map-Generator
  https://openmodeldb.info/models/1x-NormalMapGenerator-CX-Lite
  https://openmodeldb.info/models/1x-FrankenMapGenerator-CX-Lite
  Architecture: ESRGAN (Wang et al., 2018).
  Licence: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0.
  NON-COMMERCIAL USE ONLY. Texelith reads these weights and converts them to
  ONNX locally on the user's machine; the converted file is a derivative and
  stays under the same licence.

DeepBump
  Hugo Tini — https://github.com/HugoTini/DeepBump
  Model file deepbump256.onnx, downloaded from that repository.
  Licence: GNU General Public License v3.0. Texelith only downloads and runs
  the model file; no DeepBump code is included (the tiling on the torus is
  Texelith's own).

SuperMat (not downloaded by Texelith)
  Hong et al., "SuperMat: Physically Consistent PBR Material Estimation at
  Interactive Rates", ICCV 2025.
  Code: https://github.com/hyj542682306/SuperMat — weights:
  https://huggingface.co/oyiya/SuperMat. Licence: MIT.
  Its base model, Stable Diffusion 2.1, is under the CreativeML Open RAIL++-M
  licence and is downloaded by the SuperMat code on first use.
  Installed by the user with install_supermat_portable.bat into its own
  portable Python environment (supermat_env/); Texelith starts it as a
  separate process through supermat_worker.py and includes none of its code
  or weights.

Sample textures (samples/)
--------------------------
Rock064, Bricks105, PavingStones151, WoodFloor051, Metal063 — ambientCG
(https://ambientcg.com), CC0 1.0 Universal. Copied from
https://github.com/amazingsammed/mini_textures, which bundles them under CC0.

Other references
----------------
Reoriented normal mapping: Barré-Brisebois & Hill, "Blending in Detail", 2012.
OpenMW specular map layout (RGB colour, alpha × 255 = shininess) from
files/shaders/compatibility/objects.frag.
OpenMW parallax formula and normal-map conventions are taken from the OpenMW
documentation and shader sources (files/shaders/lib/material/parallax.glsl);
no OpenMW code is included. Game unit size (22.1 units per foot) as documented
by MWSE.
